@page "/packet-crafting-demo"
@using SuperUI.Components
@using SuperUI.Components.Network

<PageTitle>Packet Crafting Tool - SuperUI</PageTitle>

<div class="sg-demo-header">
    <h1>Packet Crafting Tool</h1>
    <p>Visual constructor and network packet simulator for education and security testing.</p>
</div>

<SgStack Vertical Spacing="24">
    <SgPacketCraftingTool />

    <SgCard Title="Educational Note" Subtitle="How it works">
        <SgStack Vertical Spacing="12">
            <p>
                This tool allows you to build raw network packets by defining headers for different layers of the OSI model:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>L2 (Data Link):</strong> Ethernet header with MAC addresses and EtherType.</li>
                <li><strong>L3 (Network):</strong> IPv4 header with IPs, TTL, and protocol selection.</li>
                <li><strong>L4 (Transport):</strong> TCP/UDP headers with ports and flags.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                The <strong>Simulation</strong> mode uses a virtual router/firewall logic on the server-side (C#) to analyze the packet 
                and determine if it would be accepted or dropped based on common network rules (e.g., TTL expiration, port blocking).
            </p>
        </SgStack>
    </SgCard>
</SgStack>
